# The two extraction payloads are NOT committed. Owner's decision, 2026-09-06.
#
# They are ~14 MB and carry nothing unique: their maps are byte-identical to the
# shipped package data in src/artistpath_builder/data/, and every figure derived
# from them -- coverage by band, per-field fact coverage, rejection counts -- is
# reproduced in README.md, which owns those figures.
#
# WHAT THIS COSTS, stated rather than discovered later. Regenerating them needs
# lux4_extract.py AND the 17 GB MusicBrainz dump, which is itself gitignored and
# is a rotating snapshot -- the 2026-07-29 export will not be fetchable forever.
# So on a fresh clone these cannot be rebuilt, and make_package_data.py cannot
# run. That is acceptable only because its OUTPUT is committed and is what the
# builder actually reads; the irreplaceable content is preserved there.
#
# To verify a future re-extraction reproduces this one, compare against the three
# shas in README.md section 5 rather than against these files.
dsp_links.json
artist_facts.json

*.log
__pycache__/
